==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]].
*1 [[Techn-Old Hyena]] spawns as the boss after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>.
*1 [[Professor A.]] spawns after 43.33 seconds<sup>1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Techn-Old Hyena]] spawns after 96.67 seconds<sup>2,900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The hardest part of this stage is not falling asleep. The way this stage works is that the stage's width is incredibly short, with the Doge Base nuking all of your units if you move even a little near the enemies.

The first enemy, Techn-Old Hyena, is easily beaten with a combination of [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]], [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] to block the Doge Base's [[Wave Attack]]s and [[Ancient Egg: N112 (Rare Cat)|Cat Egg Pod]] to stall Techn-Old Hyena at the start. After the next enemy, Professor A., spawns, start playing defensively and use [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]], [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] and Egg Pod alongside [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] to slowly chip him down while you wait for Bahamut to come off cooldown. When the second Hyena spawns, do your best to stall both enemies with [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Soractes]]'s Conjure, [[Boulder Cat]], and Egg Pod. Once Bahamut's off cooldown, use a combination of Bahamut and the Thunderbolt Cannon to finish both enemies off.

==Trivia==
*Newton's Fruit is a reference to the falling apple that inspired [[wikipedia:Isaac Newton|Isaac Newton]]'s gravitational theory.

